The SM7150's CSID and VFE1 clocks were incomplete too

Same fault as 0063, in the neighbouring blocks. Comparing against the sdm845,
which carries the same generation and DOES capture on mainline:

    csid_res_845     9 clocks: cpas_ahb, cphy_rx_src, slow_ahb_src, soc_ahb,
                               vfe0, vfe0_src, vfe0_cphy_rx, csi0, csi0_src
    csid_res_7150    THREE:    vfe0_csid, vfe0_cphy_rx, vfe0

    vfe_res_7150 VFE0   TWELVE clocks
    vfe_res_7150 VFE1   THREE:  vfe1, vfe1_src, vfe1_axi

The CSID was missing cpas_ahb, slow_ahb_src, cphy_rx_src, vfeN_src and
vfeN_csid_src; VFE1 was missing nine of the twelve that VFE0 on the same SoC
does ask for.

The VFE1 one is not theoretical: trying to capture through csid1 -> vfe1_rdi0
gives

    VIDIOC_STREAMON returned -1 (I/O error)

which is exactly what you expect from a block that gets neither the AXI bus nor
the CSID clock turned on.

The SM7150 device tree already declares all those names for the two VFEs and the
three CSIDs, so this needs no changes outside the driver.

(soc_ahb does not exist in the SM7150's camcc; its equivalent is cpas_ahb, which
is declared and is now actually requested.)
